  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In the current open beta, systems that use TeleportPlayer to find the player’s play space origin or move players with custom locomotion will usually cause remote clients to look jittery when moving. This can be seen in the videos in this canny. https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/874climbing-teleportplayer-3-times-per-frame-breaks-for-vr\n\n\nOf course, the TeleportPlayer action should be capable of teleporting a player remotely so that we don’t see people fly across the world if they are teleporting from one point to another. But there are numerous popular worlds using the interpolated teleport for player root tracking, climbing, and other player locomotion which are broken from the interpolation bug fix. \n\n\nSince both behaviors are desirable in different circumstances, it would be useful to have an option on the TeleportPlayer action after the Align Room To Destination option called “Remote Interpolate Teleport” or something along those lines. This would default to false, and when enabled prevent the local client from telling the remote clients that it has teleported. \n\n\nThis should allow climbing worlds to fix their content by enabling the remote interpolation option on the teleport actions and re-uploading.",
